*> Division by a literal zero: DIVIDE ... INTO, DIVIDE ... BY, and /
*> in expressions. A zero dividend, a statement with ON SIZE ERROR,
*> and a divisor that only starts with zeros are not reported.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. DIVIDES.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  TOTAL              PIC 9(5) VALUE 100.
01  RATE               PIC 9(3)V99 VALUE 2.
01  RESULT             PIC 9(5)V99.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    DIVIDE ZERO INTO TOTAL
    DIVIDE TOTAL BY 0 GIVING RESULT
    DIVIDE 0 INTO TOTAL GIVING RESULT REMAINDER RATE
    COMPUTE RESULT = TOTAL / 0.00
    COMPUTE RESULT = (TOTAL + 1) / ZEROS
    IF TOTAL / 0 > 1
        COMPUTE RESULT = RATE / +0
    END-IF
    DIVIDE 0 BY TOTAL GIVING RESULT
    COMPUTE RESULT = 0 / TOTAL
    COMPUTE RESULT = TOTAL / 0.5
    COMPUTE RESULT = TOTAL / 10
    DIVIDE TOTAL BY 0 GIVING RESULT
        ON SIZE ERROR DISPLAY "CANNOT DIVIDE"
    END-DIVIDE
    COMPUTE RESULT = TOTAL / 0
        ON SIZE ERROR MOVE 0 TO RESULT
    END-COMPUTE
    DISPLAY RESULT RATE
    GOBACK.
